k.\n   \n\n  \n\n The next step is to speak to Jack.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Title**\n Software Engineer\n   \n\n  \n\n**Salary**\n $140K \\- $250K \\+ Equity\n   \n\n  \n\n**Company Description**\n Opal Security is a $59M funded leader in AI\\-native identity governance, backed by Greylock and Battery, providing intelligent access management for enterprise leaders like Databricks and Figma.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Description**\n Join Opal Security to build AI\\-native identity governance systems that scale with enterprise chaos. As a full\\-stack engineer, you will design and ship features from concept to production, solving complex IAM challenges for Fortune 500s. You will work closely with customers to architect secure, real\\-time control planes that empower rapid innovation without compromising security.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Location**\n San Francisco, USA\n   \n\n  \n\n**Why this role is remarkable**\n* Join a hyper\\-growth team where 60% of the workforce joined since 2026, led by an elite executive team from Meta, Nutanix, and Palo Alto Networks.\n* Tackle the burgeoning \"identity moment\" by building the control plane for human, service, and AI agent identities used by industry leaders like Figma.\n* Influence the entire product lifecycle in an environment that prioritizes thoughtful engineering and creative problem\\-solving over high\\-velocity ticket completion.\n\n\n**What You Will Do**\n* Own critical product areas end\\-to\\-end, from initial architectural design to shipping production\\-ready features across the full application stack.\n* Collaborate directly with security teams at high\\-growth startups and global enterprises to validate solutions and understand real\\-world infrastructure challenges.\n* Establish engineering patterns and write foundational code that multiplies team velocity and shapes how Opal Security scales its technical infrastructure.\n\n\n**The ideal candidate**\n* Proven experience building and shipping complex, end\\-to\\-end products 